Run the container test harness in CI

There is no .github/ directory in this repository at all. That is the direct reason six
optional installers could rot until someone ran them in a container: nothing ever executed
them, and `make test` asserts none of the tools they provide.

make/test/run.sh --phase fast takes about a minute per distro and covers staging the repo,
bash -n over make/, shellcheck, the install-init.sh dispatch decision, `make init`
symlinks, `make test-symlinks` and a repo-dirty check. Running that over ubuntu,
archlinux, amazonlinux and termux on push would catch this whole class of regression for
free.

The heavier phases suit a schedule rather than per-push: --phase full is 20-60 minutes per
distro and --phase extras is 10-25.

run.sh already exits with the number of distros that reported failures, and each step
emits `##### STEP <name>` / `##### END <name> rc=<n>` plus a machine-readable summary
block, so it needs no adaptation to be used as a CI gate.
